[DONE] Make Scenes a higher class object, add a Scenes page, below Lights and above Floor Plan. Add some more defaults, like Hue. Make it look better, with a color gradient, rather than individual blocks.
  Added a Scenes nav page (between Lights and Floor Plan) listing each room's palette scenes as gradient tiles you click to apply. Extracted presets + editor + gradient rendering into components/scenes.tsx (shared with the Floor Plan room controller, which now uses gradients too). Replaced the per-color dots (PaletteDots) with a SceneSwatch gradient bar. Expanded presets to 14 Hue-style defaults (Relax, Read, Concentrate, Energize, Bright, Dimmed, Nightlight, Sunset, Tropical Twilight, Savanna Sunset, Spring Blossom, Aurora, Ocean, Forest). Frontend-only — the room-scenes API already existed. (Note: scenes remain room-scoped; did not migrate the separate global snapshot /api/scenes system.)

[DONE] Hue lights are not getting a color wheel. Lets make sure we're polling the Hue API correctly, `references/hue_api_reference.pdf` is a downloaded pdf of the login-locked hue API reference. It looks like in `capabilities` they're showing up as `color_rbg: false` - even though that is not true and on the floor planner they're showing up their true rgb.
  Root cause: capabilities were only written on the initial provider sync; SSE/poll updates rewrote last_state (color) but never capabilities, so a stale `color_rgb:false` persisted. Fix: poll/discovery LightEvents now carry full capabilities and refresh the stored row, so the flag self-heals on the next poll. (Floor plan defaulted showColor to true, which masked the bug there.)

[DONE] LED corning seems to only bend on the center of a tile. when it then transitions to another "wall", it appears on the "far" side of the wall. (like went through the wall ) if that makes sense. I'd like for it to be able to visually represent, for example, the strip running along the inner trim of a hallway.
  Root cause: the strip polyline offset every vertex by one fixed mount point, so corners bent through tile centers and a turn kept the wrong offset (the "through the wall" jump). Added a pure stripPath() helper that treats the run as a centerline and offsets it to one wall side, mitering the 90° corners so the line bends at the true tile corner and each leg hugs its own wall — like trim around a hallway. The hand (which wall) comes from the start tile's mount (n/s/e/w); ceiling-mount 'c' stays centered. Used by both rendering and hit-testing. (Verified geometry across straight/L/U/vertical/ceiling cases.)

[DONE] Rooms should be buttons (much like lights), with an on/off toggle (not buttons). Lets also make the scene creator a lot cleaner.
  Rooms: superseded by the later Lights-page redesign — each room is now a RoomBox container (framed box holding its light cards) whose header has a single VerticalToggle for the whole room plus a room-level color/brightness widget (same LightEditor as lights) that cascades to all members via the room call; lights stay individually editable. "On" = any member on; toggling/cascading is optimistic then confirmed.
  Scene creator: reworked as part of the Scenes page (components/scenes.tsx) — gradient live preview, preset swatches, explicit Save/Cancel, shared between the Scenes page and Floor Plan. (FloorPlan's room controller still has its own On/Off/Color buttons — left as-is since it's a richer per-region control; say the word to give it the toggle treatment too.)

