### 8 API for other apps  [DONE]

- API should be documented properly in the repo.
 - we generate client API keys, no rbac just full access to lights and rooms.

We expose Bifrost-abstracted "rooms" only (not provider groups), and individual lights.

Everything we can do in the UI should be available through the API - including scene support.

The Floor Plan is not available through API.

  Implemented the public /api/v1 surface (Bearer-token auth, decided with you):
  - Auth: Authorization: Bearer <key>. Keys are bfr_<64 hex>, SHA-256 hashed at rest, shown once on creation. New migration 0010_api_keys.sql; sha2 dep added.
  - Management (session-authed): GET/POST /api/api-keys, DELETE /api/api-keys/{id}. UI: Settings → "API keys" section (create with one-time reveal + copy, list with prefix/last-used, revoke).
  - Public (Bearer): GET /v1/lights, GET /v1/lights/{id}, PUT /v1/lights/{id}/state; GET /v1/rooms, PUT /v1/rooms/{id}/state; GET/POST /v1/rooms/{id}/scenes, DELETE .../{sid}, POST .../{sid}/apply. Rooms expose Bifrost rooms only (not provider groups); no floor plan.
  - No logic duplication: refactored lights.rs and rooms.rs to share pub(crate) service fns between the session UI API and /v1 (the native-group room control and scene logic are reused, not copied).
  - Docs: docs/api.md (auth, endpoints, examples, status codes). Tests: 9 new integration tests (happy paths + 401 for missing/invalid/revoked keys) + 4 apikeys unit tests.


